{"id": "EUVD-2026-80641", "enisaUuid": "50cefe48-532c-39fb-9e24-8f5aaf9a924e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: usb-audio: fix OOB write in snd_usbmidi_us122l_output()\n\nThe snd_usbmidi_us122l_output() picks a count of 2 on anything slower\nthan high speed and never relates it to ep->max_transfer.  The URB\nbuffer holds exactly max_transfer bytes, so a device declaring a one\nbyte bulk endpoint takes two bytes from snd_rawmidi_transmit(), and the\nmemset that pads the rest computes 1 - 2 in int and wraps to SIZE_MAX.\n\nOnly 0x800e and 0x800f are pinned to nine bytes.  The US-122MKII at\n0x0644:0x8021 falls to the default and takes usb_maxpacket(), which the\nUSB core only clamps downward.\n\nThe akai and novation output ops in this file were given the same guard\nrecently.  Do the same here.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5538daf2a5cc80ac3f3e913c0db045d92d995d40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a441a8e52148c91c2f2a91f42e3b9bc961a13a4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2dae0e3a59e31f78222279d544b98e747cd1fbff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d4add2b832b56f81bb0eab065ec35c610343018", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de6d252f115be887a701c09a05cdb076f3a590c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9392a2c346762ffee8edd1ba8bac50d2e24a2ed7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d81885d97cba7796d1f8edc88f2499c8296f5b9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4637ce34607f1733a34a57294966d26b263e626"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3999-x38p-c9qg", "CVE-2026-90033"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b68216d-3873-304e-9211-ad44090a94e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "030a07e441296c372f946cd4065b5d831d8dc40c <9d81885d97cba7796d1f8edc88f2499c8296f5b9"}, {"id": "27c00b9b-ad34-36a3-b6a0-87f93cde0457", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name":